# ---- Active scene surface IDs ----

There are TWO distinct ID spaces in every contact tuple:

  env_id  (global feature index, used in EVERY tuple as the env_id)
  self_id (per-object face index, used only in object channels)

  floor:
    env_id 1   = floor_feat1  (self_id 1)  [surface]
  table_short1:
    env_id 2   = table_short1_feat1  (self_id 1)  [top]
    env_id 3   = table_short1_feat2  (self_id 2)  [left]
    env_id 4   = table_short1_feat3  (self_id 3)  [front]
    env_id 5   = table_short1_feat4  (self_id 4)  [right]
    env_id 6   = table_short1_feat5  (self_id 5)  [back]
    env_id 7   = table_short1_feat6  (self_id 6)  [bottom]
  table_short2:
    env_id 8   = table_short2_feat1  (self_id 1)  [top]
    env_id 9   = table_short2_feat2  (self_id 2)  [left]
    env_id 10  = table_short2_feat3  (self_id 3)  [front]
    env_id 11  = table_short2_feat4  (self_id 4)  [right]
    env_id 12  = table_short2_feat5  (self_id 5)  [back]
    env_id 13  = table_short2_feat6  (self_id 6)  [bottom]
  white_box:
    env_id 14  = white_box_feat1  (self_id 1)  [top]
    env_id 15  = white_box_feat2  (self_id 2)  [left]
    env_id 16  = white_box_feat3  (self_id 3)  [front]
    env_id 17  = white_box_feat4  (self_id 4)  [right]
    env_id 18  = white_box_feat5  (self_id 5)  [back]
    env_id 19  = white_box_feat6  (self_id 6)  [bottom]
  yellow_box:
    env_id 20  = yellow_box_feat1  (self_id 1)  [top]
    env_id 21  = yellow_box_feat2  (self_id 2)  [left]
    env_id 22  = yellow_box_feat3  (self_id 3)  [front]
    env_id 23  = yellow_box_feat4  (self_id 4)  [right]
    env_id 24  = yellow_box_feat5  (self_id 5)  [back]
    env_id 25  = yellow_box_feat6  (self_id 6)  [bottom]

Face names are directions in the object's own frame: top / bottom = +Z / -Z,
front / back = +X / -X, left / right = +Y / -Y. Planes have a single
`surface` face.

Required channels: "left_ee", "right_ee", "left_sole", "right_sole", "white_box", "yellow_box"

The scene's initial mode (use this as mode 0):

    contact_mode_seq = {
        'left_sole' : [(1, 1)],
        'right_sole': [(1, 1)],
        'left_ee'   : [()],
        'right_ee'  : [()],
        'white_box' : [(6, 1, 1)],
        'yellow_box': [(6, 1, 1)],
    }

Movable objects (each needs its own channel): "white_box", "yellow_box"

# ---- Scoring ----

A plan scores 0 unless its final mode matches the discrete contact goal, the IK solver finds the whole plan
feasible and trajectory optimization (TO) then produces a cost.
Feasible plans are ranked by that TO cost: lower constraint violation
and smoother control rank higher. Plans identical to one already
evaluated in this run, and plans over the mode cap, also score 0.

